    "result_text": "The build is green. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the rule: **reject creating an owner when the owner's city already contains 50 or more owners, responding with 409 Conflict.**\n\nChanges, following the existing conventions in this Spring Boot app (the same pattern used for `DuplicateHouseholdException` / `DuplicateTelephoneException`):\n\n1. **New exception** \u2014 `rest/advice/CityAtCapacityException.java`: a `RuntimeException` carrying the offending city.\n\n2. **Controller check** \u2014 `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`: added a `CITY_CAPACITY = 50` constant and a `rejectWhenCityAtCapacity(...)` guard invoked during owner creation. It counts existing owners in that city case-insensitively (matching how the per-city customer-code sequence is already derived) and throws when the count is \u2265 50.\n\n3. **Exception handler** \u2014 `ExceptionControllerAdvice`: added `handleCityAtCapacityException` mapping the exception to `409 Conflict` with an `errors: [\"city\"]` body, consistent with the other conflict handlers.\n\nTest results: the provided acceptance test `coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity` (fills a fresh city to exactly 50, expects the 51st to be rejected with 409) passes, and the full suite is green \u2014 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
